direction: right

before: Before — 3 servers {
  direction: down
  a1: Server A owns arc 1
  b1: Server B owns arc 2
  c1: Server C owns arc 3
}

after: After adding Server D {
  direction: down
  a2: Server A owns arc 1 (unchanged) {
    style.fill: "#C8E6C9"
  }
  b2: Server B owns arc 2 (unchanged) {
    style.fill: "#C8E6C9"
  }
  d2: Server D owns part of arc 3 (new) {
    style.fill: "#FFCDD2"
  }
  c2: Server C owns the rest of arc 3 (smaller now) {
    style.fill: "#FFF9C4"
  }
}

before -> after: only the keys in Server D's new slice move — everything else stays put
